course: dictionary
lesson: 15534
title: Suitability: right for the job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Suitability is a noun. It tells you how right or appropriate something is for a purpose, a person or a situation. When something fits what is needed, it has good suitability.
explain: Films and games have age ratings to show their suitability for children. «The age rating on the game shows its suitability for young players.» The rating tells you whether the game fits your age.
explain: Suitability can also mean how fit someone is for a job or role. «The manager checked the suitability of each applicant for the job.» She looked at whether each person could do the job well.
explain: Two useful phrases are «suitability for» and «check the suitability». «Check the suitability of the book for your little sister» means look at whether the book is right for her.
fact: Suitability means how right or appropriate something is for a purpose, person or situation.
fact: Suitability can describe a thing, a person or a situation.
fact: Suitability also means how fit someone is for a job or role.
fact: Age ratings on films and games show their suitability for children.
fact: Useful phrases: «suitability for» and «check the suitability».
exercise: «The age rating on the game shows its suitability for children.» What does suitability mean here? | How many people play it | How expensive the game is | *How right the game is for children | How long the game lasts
exercise: «The manager checked the suitability of each applicant for the job.» What does suitability mean here? | How many friends they have | How quickly they arrived | How tall each applicant is | *How fit each applicant is for the job
exercise: «Check the suitability of the book before you lend it to your little sister.» Find and copy the word that names how right something is. | check | *suitability | book | little
test: «The teacher judged the suitability of the story for Year 5.» What does suitability mean? | How old the teacher is | How long the story is | *How right the story is for the class | How loud the story is
test: Which phrase means that something is right for a purpose? | close the door | *suitability for | ring the bell | count the chairs
exam: «The club wants to check the suitability of new members.» In this sentence, suitability means | the number of members in the club | *how right each new member is for the club | the colour of the club badge | the price of joining
